      "cause_of_death": "not reported",
      "treatment_summary": "Lymph node surgically resected at age 3; transfusion for pancytopenia at 7.5 years; hydroxychloroquine, mycophenolate mofetil, prednisone and rituximab (two 500 mg doses at age 10) added for SLE-like flares (ages 8-11); MMF discontinued and broad spectrum antibiotics at age 11 for neutropenic fevers; HCQ continued and prednisone tapered off at ages 12-14; monthly IVIG replacement started for hypogammaglobulinemia and recurrent infections; at age 15 escalation with prednisone, MMF (1,000 mg twice daily) and two 1000 mg doses of rituximab plus ongoing HCQ and monthly IVIG, with improving lymphadenopathy",
      "disease_label_as_stated": "haploinsufficiency of A20 (HA20) (presumptive); earlier provisional diagnosis of systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)",
      "clinical_diagnosis_basis": "Whole exome sequencing (after a negative NGS immunodeficiency panel of over 200 genes) identified a heterozygous de novo TNFAIP3 variant; the authors state the HA20 diagnosis is presumptive and not confirmed because no functional biochemical assays were done",
      "source_reference_in_review": "not reported",
